From: RerFire <rerfire@local>
Subject: [PATCH] rust.mk: do not auto-enable per-crate Rust LTO when --disable-lto

Mach unconditionally adds `-Clto` and `-Cembed-bitcode=yes` to the release
Rust build whenever cross-language LTO is not on. With `--disable-lto`,
`MOZ_LTO_RUST_CROSS` is unset, so this branch fires anyway and forces Rust
to emit LLVM bitcode (`*.rcgu.o`) into staticlibs.

When rustc and the C++ clang use different LLVM majors (e.g. Rust 1.95
bundles LLVM 22 while Firefox ESR 128 needs LLVM 18 for the NSS/NSPR
bindgen pipeline), the C++ linker calls libLTO and fails with:

    ld: could not parse bitcode object file libbuiltins_static.a(...):
        'Invalid attribute group entry (Producer: 'LLVM22...' Reader: 'LLVM 18...')'

Gate the auto-Rust-LTO block on `MOZ_LTO` being defined so that
`--disable-lto` truly disables LTO end-to-end. The block then only runs
when LTO was requested but the Rust side isn't doing the cross-language
flavor (i.e. C/C++ LTO only) — the original intent.

--- a/config/makefiles/rust.mk
+++ b/config/makefiles/rust.mk
@@ -85,6 +85,10 @@ endif
 ifndef DEVELOPER_OPTIONS
 ifndef MOZ_DEBUG_RUST
+# RerFire: only auto-enable per-crate Rust LTO when LTO is enabled at all.
+# Upstream enables it whenever MOZ_LTO_RUST_CROSS is unset, which forces Rust
+# bitcode into staticlibs and breaks links when rustc's LLVM != C++ clang's.
+ifdef MOZ_LTO
 # Enable link-time optimization for release builds, but not when linking
 # gkrust_gtest. And not when doing cross-language LTO.
 ifndef MOZ_LTO_RUST_CROSS
@@ -102,6 +106,7 @@ RUSTFLAGS += -Cembed-bitcode=yes
 endif
 endif
 endif
 endif
 endif
+endif  # RerFire: close MOZ_LTO guard

 ifdef CARGO_INCREMENTAL
